{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":66,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.N1_factor_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.N1_factor_one","kind":"theorem","line":728,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L728-L734","doc":"The `u⁰` coefficient of the eigenphase expansion is `1`:\n`N1_factor 1 = cos(α(1) − b(1)·ℏ_q(1)²/2) = cos 0 = 1`.\nMatches the probe's `[u^0] = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB_one","kind":"theorem","line":720,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L720-L726","doc":"Hoefsmit coupling at the classical point: `b(1) = √3/2`.\nThis value sets the eigenphase `u¹` Taylor coefficient\n`a_1 = -b(1)/6 = -√3/12` (probe `qbeta_eigenphase_taylor_in_u.py`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alpha_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alpha_one","kind":"theorem","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L715-L718","doc":"The eigenphase `α = (z−1)·h/2` vanishes at `q = 1` (since `h(1)=0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ_one","kind":"theorem","line":709,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L709-L713","doc":"Markov–Jones parameter equals `1/2` at `q = 1` — true in **both**\nconventions, since `q = 1` is their only point of contact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeH_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeH_one","kind":"theorem","line":705,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L705-L707","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹` vanishes at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ_one","kind":"theorem","line":701,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L701-L703","doc":"`ℏ_q = (q−1)/q` vanishes at the classical point `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n7_structural_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n7_structural_form","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L665-L676","doc":"**Conditional N=7 ladder form** (§3b-cond). Locks the c_7 form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n7_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n7_categorical","kind":"def","line":657,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L657-L663","doc":"N=7 ladder rung built with the TRUE (abstract) categorical `c_7`\ncoefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC7StructuralFormClass.c7_is_jones_cubed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC7StructuralFormClass.c7_is_jones_cubed","kind":"theorem","line":651,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L651-L651","doc":"Structural identity: the true categorical `c_7(q)` equals\n`J_Hopf(q=1)³ = -8` (constant, no q-dep) for all `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC7StructuralFormClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC7StructuralFormClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":648,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L648-L648","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC7StructuralFormClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC7StructuralFormClass","kind":"class","line":639,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L639-L655","doc":"**N=7 structural-form class for Q_β** (§3b-cond).\n\nAxiomatises `c_7 = J³ = -8`. The canonical instance docstring\nexplicitly labels this as **chosen for pattern aesthetics, not\nderivation** — at N=7 the residual leverage is 10⁻¹⁵ scale, so\nmany c_7 values give acceptable closure. The class locks the\naesthetic pattern; no claim of derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC7Categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC7Categorical","kind":"def","line":635,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L635-L637","doc":"Abstract true categorical N=7 coefficient `c_7(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n6_structural_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n6_structural_form","kind":"theorem","line":622,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L622-L633","doc":"**Conditional N=6 ladder form** (§3b-cond). Locks the c_6 form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n6_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n6_categorical","kind":"def","line":614,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L614-L620","doc":"N=6 ladder rung built with the TRUE (abstract) categorical `c_6`\ncoefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC6StructuralFormClass.c6_is_jones_sq_kashiwara","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC6StructuralFormClass.c6_is_jones_sq_kashiwara","kind":"theorem","line":608,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L608-L608","doc":"Structural identity: the true categorical `c_6(q)` equals\n`J_Hopf(q=1)² · b(q)²` for all `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC6StructuralFormClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC6StructuralFormClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":605,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L605-L605","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC6StructuralFormClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC6StructuralFormClass","kind":"class","line":597,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L597-L612","doc":"**N=6 structural-form class for Q_β** (§3b-cond).\n\nAxiomatises `c_6 = J²·K = 4·b²` (Jones-squared × Kashiwara b²).\n**EMPIRICAL FIT** per the canonical instance docstring — NOT a\nderivation. The class merely LOCKS the form so downstream Lean\ncan carry it as a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC6Categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC6Categorical","kind":"def","line":593,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L593-L595","doc":"Abstract true categorical N=6 coefficient `c_6(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n5_structural_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n5_structural_form","kind":"theorem","line":581,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L581-L591","doc":"**Conditional N=5 ladder form** (§3b-cond). Locks the c_5 form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n5_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n5_categorical","kind":"def","line":574,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L574-L579","doc":"N=5 ladder rung built with the TRUE (abstract) categorical `c_5`\ncoefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC5StructuralFormClass.c5_is_kashiwara_offset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC5StructuralFormClass.c5_is_kashiwara_offset","kind":"theorem","line":568,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L568-L568","doc":"Structural identity: the true categorical `c_5(q)` equals\n`-(b(q)² + 1/2)` for all `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC5StructuralFormClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC5StructuralFormClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":565,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L565-L565","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC5StructuralFormClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC5StructuralFormClass","kind":"class","line":559,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L559-L572","doc":"**N=5 structural-form class for Q_β** (§3b-cond).\n\nAxiomatises `c_5 = -(b² + 1/2)` (Kashiwara b² + Hopf-half offset);\nsub-ppt residual at canonical q₀. Same near-match status as c_3/c_4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC5Categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC5Categorical","kind":"def","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L555-L557","doc":"Abstract true categorical N=5 coefficient `c_5(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n4_structural_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n4_structural_form","kind":"theorem","line":542,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L542-L553","doc":"**Conditional N=4 ladder form** (§3b-cond, proved sorry-free from\n`QbetaC4StructuralFormClass`). Locks the c_4 = J·b⁴ form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n4_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n4_categorical","kind":"def","line":534,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L534-L540","doc":"N=4 ladder rung built with the TRUE (abstract) categorical `c_4`\ncoefficient. The N=3 factor remains the concrete Jones form (as\nin `N3_factor`); only the N=4 rung is abstract here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC4StructuralFormClass.c4_is_jones_kashiwara","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC4StructuralFormClass.c4_is_jones_kashiwara","kind":"theorem","line":528,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L528-L528","doc":"Structural identity: the true categorical `c_4(q)` equals\n`J_Hopf(q=1) · b(q)⁴` for all `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC4StructuralFormClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC4StructuralFormClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":525,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L525-L525","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC4StructuralFormClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC4StructuralFormClass","kind":"class","line":515,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L515-L532","doc":"**N=4 structural-form class for Q_β** (§3b-cond).\n\nAxiomatises the recursive pair-rules form `c_4 = J·K² = J·b⁴`\n(Jones × Kashiwara b⁴) — same status as c_3: near-match at q₀\n(0.91% empirical residual per audit), not Taylor-exact.\n\nSee `docs/audits/2026-05-30-qbeta-recursive-pair-rules-and-habiro-pde.md`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC4Categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC4Categorical","kind":"def","line":511,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L511-L513","doc":"Abstract true categorical N=4 coefficient `c_4(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n3_structural_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_n3_structural_form","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L460-L482","doc":"**Conditional N=3 ladder form** (§3b-cond, proved sorry-free from\n`QbetaC3StructuralFormClass`).\n\nGiven the structural identity `c_3 = J_Hopf`, the categorical N=3\nrung equals the explicit Jones closed form `(1 + J_Hopf·b³·ℏ_q⁶)`.\nMirrors `em_alpha_inv_full_form` (PR #1508): the class field carries\nthe conditional content, the proof is `unfold + rw`.\n\nThis LOCKS THE FORM (the way #1508 locked α_EM⁻¹) without claiming\nit is Taylor-exact — the conditional hypothesis IS the open\nstructural content. Production (`per_observable_100x_status.py`)\ndoes not consume this theorem; it wires only c_2 = -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n3_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_n3_categorical","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L451-L458","doc":"N=3 ladder rung built with the TRUE (abstract) categorical `c_3`\ncoefficient. Absent the structural-form class, `qBetaC3Categorical`\nis an open quantity; the conditional theorem below collapses it to\nthe explicit Jones form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC3StructuralFormClass.c3_is_jones_hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC3StructuralFormClass.c3_is_jones_hopf","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L446-L446","doc":"Structural identity: the true categorical `c_3(q)` equals the\nHopf-link Jones value `J_Hopf(q=1) = -2` for all `q > 0`. The\nexistence of a multi-block construction realising this identity\n(closing the 3.35% residual) is the open research target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC3StructuralFormClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC3StructuralFormClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":441,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L441-L441","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC3StructuralFormClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaC3StructuralFormClass","kind":"class","line":428,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L428-L449","doc":"**N=3 structural-form class for Q_β** (§3b-cond, mirrors\n`EmAlphaInvNextOrderBlochClass`, PR #1508).\n\nThe field axiomatises the framework's structural prediction that\nthe true categorical `c_3` equals the Hopf-link Jones value\n`J_Hopf(q=1) = -2` — the Q_β analog of #1508's `[Z₂] ∈ B₃(ℂ)`\nτ_arch image. Per the discipline note above this is a structural\nNEAR-MATCH (3.35% at canonical q₀), not a Taylor-exact derivation;\nthe class is purely conditional (no instance), and production wires\nonly the Taylor-exact c_2 = -1 rung. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC3Categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaC3Categorical","kind":"def","line":418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L418-L426","doc":"Abstract true categorical N=3 coefficient `c_3(q)`. Declared as an\nabstract symbol (no closed form) so the structural-form class below\nis non-vacuous — it cannot be discharged by `rfl`, mirroring the\nopaque `BlochWigner_unit_circle : ℝ → ℝ` axiom in PR #1508's\n`em-coupling-bring-zero-mode.lean`. Its closed form — the\nmulti-Wedderburn-block Habiro derivation — is the open research\ntarget (`docs/audits/2026-05-30-qbeta-habiro-derivation-gap-plan.md`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_inductive_categorical_closure_conjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_inductive_categorical_closure_conjecture","kind":"def","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L364-L383","doc":"**Inductive categorical closure of `c_k`** (named conditional conjecture, §3b).\n\nThe conjecture (property (1) above): for every rung `k ≥ 4`, the categorical\ncoefficient `c_k(q)` is **bar-symmetric** under `q ↔ q⁻¹`,\n\n  `∀ k ≥ 4, ∀ q > 0, c_k(q⁻¹) = c_k(q)`,\n\nconsistent with `hoefsmitB_bar_invariant`.  This is the genuine,\ncheckable content of the closure claim (the residual-ceiling property (2)\nand the no-fit categorical-source property (3) are tracked in the doc).\n\nHonest disposition: the property is *named* as a `Prop` over the coefficient\nclass — it is **not** asserted (no instance proof is produced; the open\nstate is the absence of a proof term).  This replaces the previous\n`(inst : …) → True := trivial`, which captured no categorical content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.precision_ladder_N5_canonical_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.precision_ladder_N5_canonical_compat","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L328-L342","doc":"The inductive ladder at N=5 (canonical instance) matches the\nexplicit `Q_beta_categorical` defined above. This ties the\nclass-based and explicit-bundle forms together at the depth\nthe empirical evaluation uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.precision_ladder_N3_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.precision_ladder_N3_compat","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L310-L326","doc":"The inductive ladder at N=3 matches the explicit `Q_beta_categorical`\nwhen the coefficient class fixes `c_2 = -1` and `c_3 = J_Hopf(q=1)`.\n\nThis compatibility lemma is the conditional-class hypothesis chain\npoint: any downstream proof using `Q_beta_precision_ladder N=3` can\ndrop the class instance for the explicit form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_precision_ladder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_precision_ladder","kind":"def","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L296-L308","doc":"**Inductive precision-ladder export.** Iteratively applies factors\nN=k for k=2..N to the (Form A · N=1) base, given a coefficient class\ninstance for the ladder.\n\nNote: the inductive step uses `Nk_factor` for every k ≥ 2, which\ndiffers from `N2_factor` only in that the latter has `b²` not `b^2`\ninside; they coincide because `c_2 = -1` and `b²·ℏ_q^4 = b^2·ℏ_q^{4}`.\nSee `precision_ladder_N3_compat` below for the base case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Nk_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Nk_factor","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L291-L294","doc":"N=k factor under the categorical-coefficient class, for k ≥ 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaPrecisionLadderCoeffsCanonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qBetaPrecisionLadderCoeffsCanonical","kind":"instance","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L271-L289","doc":"**Canonical instance of `QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients`** with\nthe closed forms from the 2026-05-19 audit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_7_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_7_eq","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L269-L269","doc":"N=7: c_7 = c_3³ = −8 (Jones cubed). Residual leverage is so small\nat N=7 (10⁻¹⁵ scale) that many c_7 values give acceptable closure;\nthis form is chosen for pattern aesthetics, not derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_6_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_6_eq","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L265-L265","doc":"N=6: c_6 = c_3² · b² = 4·b² (Jones-squared × Kashiwara b²; closes\n6.5× tighter than N=5). EMPIRICAL FIT — not derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_5_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_5_eq","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L262-L262","doc":"N=5: c_5 = −(b² + 1/2) (Kashiwara b² + Hopf-half offset; sub-ppt residual). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_4_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_4_eq","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L260-L260","doc":"N=4: c_4 = c_3 · b⁴ (Jones × Kashiwara, 0.91% empirical residual). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L258-L258","doc":"N=3: pure Jones, c_3 = J_Hopf(q=1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L256-L256","doc":"N=2: pure Kashiwara, factor (1 - b²·ℏ_q^4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_k_at_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.c_k_at_q","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L254-L254","doc":"The k-th rung categorical coefficient `c_k(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients.mk","kind":"ctor","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L252-L252","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients","kind":"class","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L232-L269","doc":"**Categorical coefficient class for the Q_β precision ladder.**\n\nHolds the per-rung coefficients `c_k` for the factor\n`(1 + c_k · b^k · ℏ_q^{2k})` at depth `k ≥ 2`. All rungs through N=5\nare now pinned to closed forms derived from two primitives:\n\n  - **b(q)** — Hoefsmit off-diagonal coupling (Kashiwara source)\n  - **c_3 = J_Hopf(q=1) = −2** — Hopf Jones polynomial at q=1\n    (categorical inter-block source)\n\nThe closed forms (per `2026-05-19-qbeta-all-ck-categorical-extension.md`):\n\n  c_2(q) = −1                                  (pure Kashiwara, intra-block)\n  c_3(q) = −2 = J_Hopf(q=1)                    (pure Jones, inter-block)\n  c_4(q) = c_3(q) · b⁴(q) = −2·b⁴(q)           (Jones × Kashiwara mixing)\n  c_5(q) = −(b²(q) + 1/2)                       (Kashiwara b² + Hopf-half offset;\n                                                 doc's `c_4` form, off by one rung)\n\nEach instance may extend the class with c_6, c_7, ... once their\nclosed forms are derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_categorical_precision_ladder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.q_beta_categorical_precision_ladder","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L175-L210","doc":"**Q_β categorical-derivation precision ladder export.** Bundles the\nForm A baseline + N=1..N=5 factors into the canonical export.\n\n**STALE-CLAIM CORRECTION (2026-05-30).** Earlier revisions of this\ndocstring reported \"N=3 (Hopf at q=1): +6.02 ppb (beats 7.80 ppb\n100×-exp target ✓)\". That figure was a STALE-q₀ ARTIFACT: it was\ncomputed against a pre-#1422 q₀ pin. At the current canonical q₀\n(m_p-anchored, 1.10997858…) the N=3 rung is a 3.35% near-match\n(c_3 = J_Hopf = -2 vs empirical Taylor c_3 = -2.0693), NOT a +6 ppb\nbeat of the target. The honest production status is **Q_N2 = 1279\nppb** (c_2 = -1 only); see\n`docs/audits/2026-05-30-qbeta-ck-mp-dk-deep-audit.md` and\n`qbeta-delta-tr-vs-formA.witness.json`. The N=3+ factors below\nremain as the framework's STRUCTURAL form (conditional on\n`QbetaC3StructuralFormClass`), but do NOT clear the 100× target at\ncanonical q₀ and are NOT wired to production.\n\nSource for the c_4, c_5 structural forms (near-matches, not\nderivations): `docs/audits/2026-05-19-qbeta-all-ck-categorical-extension.md`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-beta-categorical-precision-ladder","label":"prop:q-beta-categorical-precision-ladder","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-categorical-precision-ladder.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L153-L171","doc":"**b is bar-symmetric**: `hoefsmitB q⁻¹ = hoefsmitB q` for `q > 0`.\n\n`hoefsmitB q = √(q⁴+q²+1)/(q²+1)`.  Dividing radicand and\ndenominator by `q²`: `q⁻⁴+q⁻²+1 = (q⁴+q²+1)/(q²)²` and\n`q⁻²+1 = (q²+1)/q²`, so `√(·)/(·)` telescopes to the `q`-form\n(`Real.sqrt_div` splits the quotient, `Real.sqrt_sq` evaluates\n`√(q²)² = q²`).  Previously an `axiom` \"pending a `sqrt_div_eq`\nlemma in Mathlib\"; the existing `Real.sqrt_div` + `Real.sqrt_sq`\nAPI discharges it directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_categorical","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L131-L136","doc":"The **Q_β categorical-derivation precision ladder** through N=5.\nAll factors are substrate-derived closed forms in `q` (via Hoefsmit\n`b`) and the topological invariant `J_Hopf(q=1) = -2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.N5_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.N5_factor","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L123-L127","doc":"N=5 factor: `1 + c_5 · b⁵ · ℏ_q^10` with\n`c_5 = −(b² + 1/2)` (Kashiwara b² + Hopf-half offset). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.N4_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.N4_factor","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L105-L109","doc":"N=4 factor: `1 + c_4 · b⁴ · ℏ_q^8` with\n`c_4 = J_Hopf(q=1) · b⁴ = −2·b⁴`. So the factor is\n`1 − 2·b⁴ · b⁴ · ℏ_q^8 = 1 − 2·b⁸·ℏ_q^8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.N3_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.N3_factor","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L90-L94","doc":"N=3 factor: `1 + J_Hopf(q=1) · b³ · ℏ_q^6 = 1 − 2 b³ ℏ_q^6`. The\nHopf-link Jones value at q=1 is the categorical contribution from\ninter-Wedderburn-block coupling at 3-fold Markov closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.N2_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.N2_factor","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L84-L86","doc":"N=2 factor: `1 − b² · ℏ_q^4` from Kashiwara `f̃_1†f̃_1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.N1_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.N1_factor","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L78-L80","doc":"N=1 factor: `cos(α − b·ℏ_q²/2)` from Kashiwara `f̃_1` eigenphase shift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_form_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_beta_form_A","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L72-L74","doc":"Form A baseline of `Q_β` per `prop:neutron-qvalue-symbolic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfClassicalLimit","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L67-L70","doc":"Classical-limit Hopf-link Jones value at `q = 1`: `J_Hopf(1) = -2`.\nThis is the unreduced Jones polynomial of the 2-component Hopf\nlink evaluated at q = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L63-L65","doc":"Hoefsmit off-diagonal coupling `b = √(q⁴ + q² + 1) / (q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alpha","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L60-L61","doc":"Single-wrap eigenphase `α = (z − 1) h / 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeH'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeH'","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L57-L58","doc":"Quantum-integer differential `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ'","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L42-L55","doc":"Markov-Jones parameter in **convention D**, `z = q³/(q² + 1)`.\n\n**Migrated from convention C 2026-08-26 (bean `qou-cxjq`).** This read\n`1/(√q + 1/√q)` = `√q/(q+1)`, convention C.\n\nAGENTS.md flags this ladder as convention-C-frame throughout, so the\nexpectation going in was that its results would not survive. The `q = 1`\nresults DO survive, and for a reason worth stating: `q = 1` is the single\npoint where the two conventions agree, both equal to `1/2`\n(`QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD_one` / `markovZC_one`). So a theorem evaluated only\nat the classical point is convention-agnostic by accident of sitting exactly\non the coincidence — not because the ladder is convention-free. Anything\nevaluated away from `q = 1` still needs re-deriving under D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ'","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean#L39-L40","doc":"Quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = (q − 1) / q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}